course: dictionary
lesson: 4545
title: Words for a cosy room
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: A hearthrug is a rug on the floor in front of a fireplace. You may not have one at home, but the words around it can help you work out what it means. Read this line from an old story: «Alice's Right Foot, Esq., Hearthrug, near the Fender».
explain: It is a made-up address on a parcel. Esq. is a polite title written on letters to a gentleman, so the hearthrug must be a place in the house. The fender is the low metal guard around a fire, so the hearthrug is close to the fire too.
explain: Try the test: put your meaning into the sentence in place of the hard word. A rug in front of the fire fits the address and makes sense. Now you know what a hearthrug is, and you can use the same method for any new word.
fact: A hearthrug is a rug laid on the floor in front of a fireplace.
fact: The hearth is the floor part of a fireplace, and a rug is a mat, so the word tells you where the rug goes.
fact: «Esq.» is short for Esquire, a polite title on letters to a gentleman.
fact: A fender is the low metal guard around a fire that keeps logs and sparks in.
fact: Hearthrugs often appear in stories of cosy homes with open fires, so they tell the reader a scene is warm, safe and homely.
exercise: «Alice's Right Foot, Esq., Hearthrug, near the Fender» What is a hearthrug? | A tall chair by the window | A small bed for a cat | A metal guard round a fire | *A rug laid on the floor in front of a fireplace
exercise: In the same address, what is a fender? | A bag for carrying logs | A thick curtain on a door | A polite title for a gentleman | *The low metal guard around a fire
exercise: A story describes a room with a hearthrug and a crackling fire. What feeling does this suggest? | Cold, empty and dangerous | Noisy and crowded with traffic | Bright and busy like a shop | *Cosy, warm and safe
test: Which word in the address is a polite title on letters to a gentleman? | Hearthrug | Alice | *Esq. | Fender
test: The hearthrug is near the fire, so where would you most likely find one? | *On the floor in front of the fireplace | On the ceiling above the table | Under the bed upstairs | In a cupboard full of plates
exam: Jayden asks, "What is a hearthrug?" Which answer is right? | A kind of cold drink served with supper | A big bird that lives near the fire | A rug in front of the fireplace | *A rug in front of the fireplace, but only in the bedroom
